        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Bipolarity defines the Blue Jays' July 4 in Seattle, where the team lived up to its name by swinging from a masterful shutout to a historic collapse. <strong>After Dylan Cease spun seven scoreless innings to blank the Mariners 2-0, the Jays imploded the very next day, surrendering 11 unanswered runs in a boat race to Randy Arozarena's grand slam and Logan Gilbert's dominance.</strong> Now sitting at 42-47 and third in the AL East, 11.5 games behind the division leader, the squad is on a one-game losing streak despite a recent win streak that included a 9-3 rout of the Mets. The story right now is Cease, whose 137 strikeouts through 16 starts set a franchise record, even as Guerrero Jr. famously declined an All-Star invite while Varland and Cease head to the game. <strong>What to watch: tonight's 5:00 PM ET rematch at Mariners Park, where Cease seeks redemption and the Jays must prove they can avoid another 11-run disaster.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 5, 2026"
      },
